 "title": "Learning removes a class-forced dissonance only by winding around a handle",
 "subject": "What changing the signs of the knot's law can do on a torus whose law is in a sign class that no state satisfies",
 "conclusion": "On a torus whose Kasteleyn law is in a class no state satisfies, the least dissonance is one violated line and one over-agreeing face, and learning at the dissonance with the state fixed removes it, leaving no even face. Every process that removes it changes the law by a cycle of nonzero homology class, so learning carries the law's class, which no change of state can, and only around a handle.",
